# Architecture (always apply)

This is a **taxi booking Next.js app** (public wizard + admin + driver + partner). Follow this file on every change. Do not invent a different stack, dump logic into one file, or wander into unrelated refactors.

## Stack (do not change unless asked)

- Next.js App Router + React 19 + TypeScript + Tailwind v4 + shadcn/ui
- MongoDB + Mongoose (`connectDB()` from `@/shared/db`)
- NextAuth v4 (`src/features/auth/lib/options.ts`) — no parallel JWT/auth library
- Zod 4 · next-intl · Stripe + MultiSafepay · Google Maps · Nodemailer

Do not introduce Hono, Drizzle, Better Auth, Expo, or a `backend/` folder.

## File size (hard rule)

- One concern per file. Target **under 150 lines**. Split before **200**.
- Never grow a god file (routes + validation + DB + UI in one place).
- New feature = new small files in the right folder. If you edit a file already over 200 lines, extract the touched concern.

```
# BAD
src/app/api/booking/route.ts

# GOOD
src/app/api/booking/route.ts                                    # HTTP only
src/features/booking/lib/create-cash-booking.service.ts         # business rules
src/features/booking/lib/booking.repo.ts                        # mongoose queries
src/features/booking/schema/cash-booking.schema.ts              # zod
```

## Layout (keep this shape)

```
src/app/[locale]/          # pages — thin
src/app/api/               # route handlers — HTTP + status
src/features/<domain>/     # ui, hooks, lib, model, schema, email
src/shared/                # ui, db, i18n, style, generic lib (no feature imports)
messages/                  # i18n dictionaries
```

- Pages compose. Hooks live in `src/features/<domain>/hooks/`. Route handlers do not price, send mail, or talk to Stripe directly — call `src/features/payments/lib/` or a domain service.
- shadcn primitives stay in `src/shared/ui/`. Do not edit them to add business UI.
- Match existing names and imports. Stay on the requested task.
